From 0a328847e39b01207c22d174804c0744639a01a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:57:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sdp: add minimal Nike-L (SDP1412) DRM/KMS display driver
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Build 070 patch 0015.  Ported from the Samsung GPL sdp_logo_nike module
(tztv-media-nike/sdp_logo_nike, kernel 4.1.10) to the Linux 6.6 DRM/KMS
framework.

The driver drives the GP (graphic-plane) layer through the on-chip mixer
at 1920×1080, inheriting the mixer / QE / POST / TMG register state the
Tizen boot firmware has already set.  Minimum viable approach:

  - Maps 7 register regions from the DT bootlogo node (OSD, GP, MIXER,
    QE, GA, POST, TMG at 0x5d0000 … 0xc00000, from firmware dtb0
    sha256 0189cc94 and GPL sdp_logo_chip.h _NIKEL_GFX_).
  - Reads the GP framebuffer physical address from /sdp_mmap
    "samsung,gfx0" (0xfb580000, 16 MiB, same sdp_logo_parse_exe_mem
    pattern).
  - Programs GP plane: H_OFFSET, INPUT_SIZE, OUTPUT_SIZE, HOR/VER_RATIO
    (0x8000 = 2:1 for UHD), GP_BASE_ADDR_LOW, enables DISP_MODE_0.
  - Handles vsync via mixer IRQ (GIC SPI 47 / 0x2f); acks by
    read-then-write-back of MIX_IRQ_STATUS (GPL vsync_irq_handler).
  - drm_simple_display_pipe + drm_gem_dma + drm_fbdev_dma.

DT: add drm@5d0000 node (samsung,sdp-drm, status=disabled) inside
soc@0 in sdp-nikel.dtsi; add root-level sdp_mmap node with
samsung,gfx0/gfx1 from firmware.

Register offsets: sdp_logo_chip.h (_NIKEL_GFX_ section, REG(x)=x<<2).
Mixer init values: sdp_logo_gfx.c (sdp_logo_gfx_init, _NIKEL_GFX_).
Plane sequence: sdp_logo.c (sdp_logo_set_plane, _NIKEL_GFX_).
All addresses from firmware dtb0 sha256 0189cc94 and GPL source only.

NEVER FLASH – compile-only until validated on the runner.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
